+/**
+ * G10-PANEL — THE SERVED `frontGate` ON A TRUE PANEL, IN THIS ENGINE (pass 8, registry-v7 §2.7a).
+ * The driven clock above is a timer and jitters, so it cannot stand for a vsync-quantised panel.
+ * This row loads the served tree's own module (the dev server's graph, no copy) and drives it with
+ * EXACT frame streams — k·(1000/Hz) ms, stamped whole-ms and fine — one non-forced write per frame
+ * on its frame's time, the way `frontTween` writes. The gate's grain detector is the ENGINE's own
+ * (`performance.now()` inside `write`), so WebKit reads its whole-millisecond clock for real.
+ * Asserts: a 60 Hz stream keeps EVERY frame (≥ 59/s: pass 7's whole-ms +1 re-cut WebKit at 40.2/s
